From 562cf024e7c99208624c6f3f26f73e14073b6a07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:11:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(slack-bot): allow choosing the Claude Agent harness for
 Slack

Add a workspace-level `harness` to the Slack integration settings so
operators can run Slack-created sessions on Claude Agent. Unset keeps
the current behavior (OpenCode, no harness sent to the control plane).

- shared: `slackGlobalSettingsSchema` gains an optional `harness`.
- control-plane: Slack settings validation accepts `harness` at the
  global level only, rejects unknown ids, and rejects a default model
  the harness cannot run via `checkHarnessCompatibility`.
- slack-bot: the launcher resolves the harness (recovery plan, then the
  Slack setting, then the default), checks the session and first-prompt
  models against it before creating anything, sends it on session
  create, and stores it on the thread mapping. Stale-thread recovery
  keeps the thread's harness (legacy mappings stay on OpenCode), and a
  follow-up `!model` the thread's harness cannot run is answered with
  the reason instead of being sent.
- web: an "Agent harness" picker in Slack settings; the default-model
  list is filtered to the harness and an incompatible pair blocks Save.
- docs: CLAUDE_AGENT.md, Slack and agent-harness pages, changelog.

Closes #2044
