+### Slack
+
+Administrators choose the harness for Slack-created sessions under **Settings > Integrations >
+Slack > Agent harness**. Unset, Slack keeps creating OpenCode sessions.
+
+- The choice applies to **new** sessions. A thread keeps the harness its session started on, and a
+  thread whose session has expired is recovered on that same harness, even if the setting has since
+  changed.
+- Claude Agent runs Anthropic models only, and Slack has several model sources: the Slack default
+  model in settings, `DEFAULT_MODEL`, each user's App Home model, and `!model` flags. Saving a Slack
+  default model the chosen harness cannot run is refused. Any other source that resolves to a
+  non-Anthropic model is answered in the thread with the reason (for example
+  `Model "openai/gpt-5.4" cannot run on the Claude Agent harness.`) instead of creating a session or
+  sending the prompt.
+- Slack sessions have no per-session account picker, so on Claude Agent they authenticate like any
+  other session without an explicit selection: the installation default Claude account when one is
+  set, otherwise `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.
+- Claude Agent sessions need a sandbox image that includes it (see **Image** below); roll out new
+  images before switching Slack over.
+
