+### Agent harness
+
+Choose the [agent harness](/models/agent-harnesses) for new Slack-started sessions under **Agent harness**: **OpenCode** (the default) or **Claude Agent**. The choice applies to new sessions only; a thread keeps the harness it started on, including when an expired session is replaced.
+
+Claude Agent runs Anthropic models only. With it selected, the **Default model** list shows only models it can run, and a default model it cannot run cannot be saved. If a user's App Home model or a `!model` flag names a model the harness cannot run, the bot replies in the thread with the reason, for example `Model "openai/gpt-5.4" cannot run on the Claude Agent harness.`, and no session is created or prompt sent.
+
 ### Session instructions
 
 Set workspace-wide instructions under **Session Instructions**. They are appended to the first prompt of every new Slack-started session as an `## Additional Instructions` section, for standing guidance such as coding standards, preferred tools, or PR conventions. They apply to new sessions only, and are limited to 10,000 characters. Linear has the equivalent **Issue Session Instructions**.
